course: dictionary
lesson: 9756
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words change their meaning depending on the situation. Supper is one of them. Its main meaning is the evening meal, or a light meal eaten last thing before bed. In «The Mole's thoughts ran a good deal on supper», the word tells you Mole was thinking about food in the evening.
explain: Context gives you the clue. In «Toad hunts out cold chicken, trifle and lobster salad» for supper, the list of food shows it is a proper meal. In «Supper's here at last, hooray!» Toad is pleased that the meal has arrived. Ask yourself: what kind of meal is this, and when does it happen?
explain: Families can use words differently. In some parts of northern England, tea is the evening meal and supper is a snack before bed. In the USA and Canada, supper and dinner are often the same. So if someone says «We eat supper at six», check what they mean before you guess.
fact: Supper means the evening meal, especially a light or simple one.
fact: Supper can also mean the last meal before bed.
fact: In some UK families and regions, supper means the main evening meal, the same as dinner or tea.
fact: «The Last Supper» was the meal Jesus shared with his disciples the night before he died.
fact: «A fish supper» in Scotland means fish and chips.
exercise: «Christians remember the Last Supper in Holy Communion.» Which kind of supper is this? | A light meal eaten before bed | A snack in northern England | A fish supper in Scotland | *A special meal shared by Jesus and his disciples
exercise: «Mole goes out to check on the stoat sentries; Badger wants supper.» What does Badger want? | A new hat | A bath | A letter | *The evening meal
exercise: «Sing for your supper» means you | Sing a song at dinner | Go to bed hungry | Eat before you sing | *Do something in return for help
test: In «After a fine supper the Woman looks at a mutton blade-bone», what is the most likely meaning of supper? | *The evening meal | A picnic in the woods | A sweet pudding | A snack in the morning
test: Ella's gran from Edinburgh says, «Let's get a fish supper.» What does she mean? | A fish cooked for breakfast | Fish on a plate with no chips | *Fish and chips | A fish that sings
exam: In the USA, what does supper most likely mean when a family says «We eat supper at six»? | A piece of toast before school | *The main evening meal | Only a cup of tea | A church service
